  "_doc": "43A season scripts. day01 marks. trickle = extra customer waves (first wave is always at day 0). scamKind: npc | baron | null. forceEvent overrides pickEvent. novelty.at is also a mark (season:novelty). Rule: no mark kind equals the previous season's same mark (|d| >= 0.02). endless rotates rows 6..10 (43D: the wrap S10→S11=row 6 also obeys the gap rule; raidDouble novelty ARMS the S6 wave 0.04 day before it lands). See LUMEN_extras/game/docs/HANDOFF_43Z.md. 44C demand: { stallKind: mult } on S2–S10 (S1 none). Exactly one mult ≥ 1.3 = HOT, one ≤ 0.7 = COLD; 0.3 ≤ mult ≤ 2; hot/cold differ from the previous season (incl. the S10→S11 rotate wrap). fair price × mult (economy.stallInfo) and PREFS weight × mult (customers) at read time. T4 (S57) strangers: [{at, kind: 'fair'|'scam'}] = friendly strangers that walk in from the pier (scamNpc.js). 'scam' = the next scam the player has not met yet (all six, then a remix); 'fair' = a genuinely good deal. One in three or more is fair so refusing everything is not optimal. The older `scam`/`scamKind` marks stay (npc → also a stranger scam; baron → the Baron's own visit).",
